{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 formalization of V. Šverák, \"Rank-one convexity does not imply quasiconvexity\", Proc. Roy. Soc. Edinburgh Sect. A 120 (1992), 185-189: a quartic polynomial F on 3x2 matrices that is rank-one convex but not quasiconvex, and its lift to m x n matrices for m >= 3 and n >= 2, which answers Morrey's problem negatively for maps with at least three components.\n\nEvery result of the paper is proved by the paper's argument: Lemma 1 (quasiconvexity of a continuous function is tested by periodic maps), the structure of the subspace L and the computation (4), Lemma 2 (the extension of f from L to a rank-one convex F), the Theorem, the Remark (F is a polynomial of degree four) and the Corollary. Nothing is assumed, and the proofs use only Mathlib. The repository formalizes other papers on Morrey's problem too, each its own submission.",
  "authors": [
